"Where is AI?"

Students identify AI systems they interact with every day and classify:
  What the AI does
  What data it uses
  What business problem it solves
  Who benefits
  What could go wrong


  An AI system that I interact with almost everyday is the Penn State AI studio which uses Chat-GPT and Claude. The AI is a
generative chatbot that I use to check answers and ask questions that I have. It uses data from all over the internet, which
can make it unreliable at times. It solves the business problem of having to scroll through lots of items through google or
other search engines and instead you can read a summary for a quicker answer. The people who benefit are students and users who
are looking for quick and easily understood answers to questions. It also helps students to check their answers on assignemnts
before having to submit them for a final grade. One thing that could go wrong is that students will use the chat bots only for
answers to assignments and will not learn the content. This would be considered cheating and would cause students to not learn
the materials they need to know for their future careers.
